@startuml 03_cliente_servidor_pool
title Arquitetura 3: Cliente-Servidor com Pool de Threads (N=2)

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<server>> #FFD966
  BackgroundColor<<thread>> #D9D2E9
  BackgroundColor<<client>> #9FC5E8
  BackgroundColor<<wait>> #EFEFEF
  BorderColor black
}

rectangle "SERVIDOR\nPool fixo: N = 2 threads" as S <<server>> {
  rectangle "Thread 1\n(reutilizável)" as T1 <<thread>>
  rectangle "Thread 2\n(reutilizável)" as T2 <<thread>>
}

rectangle "Cliente 1\n(onda 1)" as C1 <<client>>
rectangle "Cliente 2\n(onda 1)" as C2 <<client>>
rectangle "Cliente 3\n(onda 2 - fila)" as C3 <<wait>>
rectangle "Cliente 4\n(onda 2 - fila)" as C4 <<wait>>

T1 -down-> C1 : onda 1
T2 -down-> C2 : onda 1
C3 .down.> T1 : espera liberar
C4 .down.> T2 : espera liberar

note bottom of S
  N threads fixos; excesso de clientes
  espera em fila até thread liberar.
  Tempo total = ceil(clientes / N) × tempo individual
end note

@enduml
